    "_comment": "GROK · The world model's CSV read back as a LOG (one column per line) and split with TableFrame.grok: the field split itself, what the ColumnDefinition schema controls (output name, dtype, column order), the null contract for lines a pattern does not match, and the messy-line patterns (%{GREEDYDATA}/%{DATA}, quoted fields, an Expr instead of a column name). Every test is a pub->tfr->sub chain over gk_src (LocalFileSrc with SrcFileFormat.LOG, reading one staged world CSV as LINES: columns `file` + `message`) / gk_ops (@transformer, applies the grok calls under test) / gk_sink (TrashDest, asserts the parse and discards). polars has no grok, so the expectations are authored against the world sample data's known content and are checked offline too (see functions/_harness.py, validate.py). Generated by gen_suites.py."
